# Design System

- One neutral base color + one accent color, used consistently for
  every primary action and active state. Status colors (red/green)
  only for real state (unfilled shift / confirmed) — never decorative.
- One sans-serif type family, small consistent type scale, generous
  whitespace. This is a daily-use operational tool, not a marketing
  site — restraint over decoration.
- Manager screens: sidebar dashboard (shadcn Sidebar component), one
  clear primary action per screen, dense-but-clear tables/grids.
- Worker-facing public page (/app/s/[linkToken]): centered single
  column, max-width ~480px, no sidebar, no app chrome, mobile-first.
  Progressive disclosure — don't show time pickers for a day until
  the worker toggles it available.
- Never: gradients, ALL-CAPS eyebrow labels, emoji-as-icons, identical
  heavy-shadow cards stacked everywhere, decorative animation.
- An under-filled/problem state must be the single most visually
  obvious element on any screen it appears on. A fully-correct state
  should look calm, not celebratory.
